A||||9||Philphine||listening to fuel pump with key turned to on||||1||
Z||000000||Philphine||08-31-2001||07:35 PM||||<BR>should i hear anything else spooling up beside the fuel pump when the key is turned to on?<P> i am playing with an '86 gt i got today. i was told it needed a fuel pump. i had to change the battery and then i disconnected the coil to distributer wire to let it turn over a second or two and not start (hadn't been started for over a year to a year and a half). then i sprayed some quick start in the throttle body opening to see if it would fire, but i got nothing. since it wouldn't fire at all i thought to check the fuel pump fuse but it's good. then i concentrated on listening and when i turn the key i hear the fuel pump i guess. what else might it be?<P> i know it could still be clogged injectors or the pump working but weak. but if nothing else should be running in the on position i'm thinking i should switch over to checking for a spark. thanks for any help. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||08-31-2001||08:58 PM||||Sounds like good news to me!<BR>The mechanical expertise of a pawn shop is sometimes questionable. <BR>It should fire with the starter fluid. Hearing the fuel pump is a good sign.<BR>I'd much rather change an ignition module than a fuel pump.<BR>Check and insure spark first. Then check fuel pressure. <BR>Good luck with your diagnosis.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||09-01-2001||09:14 AM||||thanks wolfhound, they said they'd had a nearby mechanic look at it and he told them it was the fuel pump. sure i'm not hearing something else? i thought there was a thing or two else that set themselves when the key is turned on.   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||09-01-2001||09:25 AM||||Philphine, Nothing else I know of. Turn the ignition on to load fuel pressure. Turn off ignition. If you don't have a pressure guage,  take the cap off the shrader valve (same as tire valve) right behind the thermostate housing on the fuel rail. Depress the center pin if it sprays gas you have a working fuel pump. Be careful doing this, no open flame , watch your eyes etc. Just push it quick to check for pressure. It want tell how much pressure but it will indicate if it's running or not.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 09-01-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000004||dgroves||09-01-2001||10:41 AM||||Check out Oliver's Fiero page for the "Pre Flight" check. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||09-01-2001||12:24 PM||||ok thanks. thats what i needed to know. and also for letting me know about the valve on the fuel rail. this is the first v6 i've looked at beyond passing so i'm not familiar with anything under the hood (trunk? trood? hunk?) ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mark||09-01-2001||12:47 PM||||You may also hear the heater/AC blower running (as well as the radiator fan and rear compartment blower, if the AC is on).||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wolfhound||09-01-2001||02:01 PM||||Let us know how it goes! I,ll watch the post periodicly and offer any advise I fill confident to give.<BR>Mark I think he would recognise those sounds, he's just new to the V6.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Philphine||09-01-2001||04:03 PM||||got it running. it ended up being electrical afterall. i took the dist. cap off and the contact points were pretty corroded. filed on them some with no results. sprayed it and the dist. works with contact cleaner and it started right up. it runs kind of rough (not real bad but i can just kind of hear a lope), check engine light came on and it got hot after about 10 min. idling. that scares me most, but checked oil, no antifreeze. will check anitfreeze when it cools down. i'm crossing my fingers for maybe a stuck thermostat from sitting or something simple. the over flow is full but cool. the gas dosen't smell like varnish but it dosen't exactly smell fresh, so i topped it off with fresh gas and a couple of bottles of gas treatment for when i run it again.<P>i know i'll need to get a new dist. cap (amoung other things) but for now i'm happy. i'd rather be trying to get a car to run better than trying to figure out why it's not running at all. thanks everyone, and be prepared for plenty (with a capital PLENTY) of dumb questions to come.<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Wolfhound||09-01-2001||05:30 PM||||My next step here would be to change plugs.||||reg||14
